<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Food Bureau buys 15,470 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Food Bureau buys 15,470 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Provincial Food Bureau bought on Wednesday a 15,470-tonne shipment of U.S. No. 1 wheat, grain traders said.  </p>
<p>Traders said the Food Bureau tendered the wheat on behalf of Taiwan's armed forces and such tenders are usually placed quietly once a year.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a FOB basis from Agrex, traders said.</p>
<p>Details of the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Type		  Tonne   Date/Location    Prices</p>
<p>				   Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> Hard Red Winter   7,700   Oct  1-20	  U$204.75</p>
<p> Soft Wheat	  7,770			  U$193.75</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
